# Production Caddyfile — Debian target.
#
# No TLS configuration is needed. Caddy 2.5+ recognises a *.ts.net site address
# and fetches the certificate from the local tailscaled over its unix socket,
# which docker-compose.yml mounts in. Requirements on the target:
#
#   - HTTPS Certificates and MagicDNS enabled for the tailnet in the Tailscale
#     admin console. Without these no certificate can be issued at all.
#   - CADDY_DOMAIN set to the machine's fully qualified tailnet name.
#   - Caddy reachable only on the tailnet — enforced by publishing its ports to
#     CADDY_BIND_ADDR (the tailnet IP), not 0.0.0.0.
#
# Fallback if the socket route misbehaves: run `tailscale cert` on the host to
# write cert and key files, mount them read-only, and add an explicit
# `tls <cert> <key>` to each site block in sites.caddy.

import sites.caddy
